WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.839
Part seven: History. Every change in SimplyFile is kept - what each field was, what it became, when, and who made it. Replaced documents are kept too, so any earlier version can be downloaded.

2
00:00:16.438 --> 00:00:24.838
Ramesh Iyer's details. His father's name was entered with a spelling mistake, and he has a new mobile number.

3
00:00:25.438 --> 00:00:28.078
Correct them, and save.

4
00:00:31.171 --> 00:00:34.871
Open the client again, and press History.

5
00:00:35.484 --> 00:00:44.964
One save is one entry: who made it, where and when, and every field it changed - what it was, struck through, and what it is now.

6
00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:51.938
Below it, everything since the client was added, newest first - grouped by day.

7
00:00:52.546 --> 00:01:00.946
Details and Documents can be seen apart, and any field, value or person can be searched - say, the phone.

8
00:01:02.953 --> 00:01:13.533
Shree Ganesh Agarwal H U F's statement was replaced in part one, when the corrected one came in. The first version was not thrown away.

9
00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:23.960
History shows the document replaced, version one by version two - and version one can be downloaded, exactly as it was first uploaded.

10
00:01:24.578 --> 00:01:34.058
The same History button is on Intake and map, Reconcile, Compute and close, and the Tax audit - each showing this client's changes.

11
00:01:34.671 --> 00:01:43.601
The firm has its own History, on My firm: the firm's details, and its team - people added, and every change of role.

12
00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:52.343
So when someone asks who changed a role, or what a P A N used to be, the answer is one click away.

13
00:01:52.969 --> 00:02:10.009
History: every field, old and new, who and when, and every earlier document kept. What is logged, what each field is called, and how long it is kept are SimplyFile's own rules, kept as chips. Thank you for watching.
